{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IntervalTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The intervals are kept in an AVL tree ordered by lower bound, then upper bound, then the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were inserted in, and each vertex also records the largest upper bound in its subtree, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a search skips every subtree that ends before the query begins (Cormen, Leiserson, Rivest and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Stein, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Introduction to Algorithms","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", §14.3). The same interval may be stored more than once,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with different values."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var meetings = IntervalTree<Int, String>()","meetings.insert(9 ..< 10, value: \"stand-up\")","meetings.insert(10 ..< 12, value: \"design review\")","meetings.insert(11 ..< 13, value: \"lunch\")","meetings.containing(11).map(\\.value)          \/\/ [\"design review\", \"lunch\"]","meetings.overlapping(9 ..< 11).map(\\.value)   \/\/ [\"stand-up\", \"design review\"]","meetings.contained(in: 9 ..< 12).map(\\.range) \/\/ [9 ..< 10, 10 ..< 12]"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intervals are half-open, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"9 ..< 10"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"10 ..< 12"},{"type":"text","text":" touch without overlapping. As a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection, the tree’s elements are its entries in that order, read by in-order position."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/rangetrees\/intervaltree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"RangeTrees"}],"externalID":"s:10RangeTrees12IntervalTreeV","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"IntervalTree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IntervalTree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IntervalTree"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree.swift#L26","fileName":"IntervalTree.swift"}},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/ST"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/Entry","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/Iterator","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/SearchView"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/init()","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation